<div class="su-g-accordion-faqs aem-GridColumn aem-GridColumn--default--12">













<div class="ab-g-list-exp section">
	<ul class="su12-accordion-faqs  " role="list">
		
			
			
			<li class="su12-accordion-faqs__item on" an-tr="su12_accordion faqs-product family showcase-cta-content_click" an-ca="content click" an-ac="feature" an-la="faq:accordion:what are the newest and latest samsung mobile products" role="listitem">
				<h3>
					<a href="javascript:void(0)" class="su12-accordion-faqs__title" aria-expanded="true" role="button">
						
						<div class="su12-accordion-faqs__title-text">What are the newest and latest Samsung mobile products?</div>
						<span class="icon-wrap">
							<svg class="icon plus" focusable="false"><use xlink:href="#plus-bold" href="#plus-bold"></use></svg>
							<svg class="icon minus" focusable="false"><use xlink:href="#minus-bold" href="#minus-bold"></use></svg>
						</span>
					</a>
				</h3>
				<div class="su12-accordion-faqs__contents" id="anchor-id00">
					<div class="su12-accordion-faqs__contents-description">During the latest Unpacked on February 25, 2026, Samsung was pleased to release a wide range of innovative new products including the Galaxy S26 Series and new Galaxy Buds. 
<br />
<br />• The newest S Series smartphones are Galaxy S26 Ultra, Galaxy S26+ and Galaxy S26, which combine slim design with next-gen performance and convenient AI assistance. You can maximize your Galaxy experience with the Galaxy Buds4 Pro and Galaxy Buds4, featuring a reimagined blade design and clear delivery of Hi-Fi sound.
<br />
<br />• Enhance your productivity and daily life with the latest Galaxy Watch models, the Galaxy Watch8 series, which includes Galaxy Watch8, Galaxy Watch8 Classic and Galaxy Watch8 Ultra, providing AI support and wellness tracking right from your wrist.</div>
					
					
						
					<!--
						<div class="su12-accordion-faqs__contents-disclaimer-wrap">
							<p class="su12-accordion-faqs__contents-disclaimer">...omitted...</p>
						</div>-->
						
					

					
				</div>
			</li>
		
			
			
			<li class="su12-accordion-faqs__item " an-tr="su12_accordion faqs-product family showcase-cta-content_click" an-ca="content click" an-ac="feature" an-la="faq:accordion:what is privacy display and how can i use it" role="listitem">
				<h3>
					<a href="javascript:void(0)" class="su12-accordion-faqs__title" aria-expanded="false" role="button">
						
						<div class="su12-accordion-faqs__title-text">What is Privacy Display and how can I use it?</div>
						<span class="icon-wrap">
							<svg class="icon plus" focusable="false"><use xlink:href="#plus-bold" href="#plus-bold"></use></svg>
							<svg class="icon minus" focusable="false"><use xlink:href="#minus-bold" href="#minus-bold"></use></svg>
						</span>
					</a>
				</h3>
				<div class="su12-accordion-faqs__contents" id="anchor-id114">
					<div class="su12-accordion-faqs__contents-description">The world's first smartphone Privacy Display is a built-in privacy screen on Galaxy S26 Ultra that uses innovative technology to protect your device's display from prying eyes in public places.
<br /><br />• When activated, the screen's pixels move dynamically to protect your private information by obscuring what's on your screen from view.
<br /><br />• Choose to have the full screen hidden at all times or customize further and have it activate when selected apps are in use or when you receive certain notifications that you want to keep private.<sup>1</sup></div>
					
					
						
					<!--
						<div class="su12-accordion-faqs__contents-disclaimer-wrap">
							<p class="su12-accordion-faqs__contents-disclaimer">...omitted...</p>
						</div>-->
						
					

					
				</div>
			</li>
		
			
			
			<li class="su12-accordion-faqs__item " an-tr="su12_accordion faqs-product family showcase-cta-content_click" an-ca="content click" an-ac="feature" an-la="faq:accordion:which galaxy smartphones have big displays" role="listitem">
				<h3>
					<a href="javascript:void(0)" class="su12-accordion-faqs__title" aria-expanded="false" role="button">
						
						<div class="su12-accordion-faqs__title-text">Which Galaxy smartphones have big displays?</div>
						<span class="icon-wrap">
							<svg class="icon plus" focusable="false"><use xlink:href="#plus-bold" href="#plus-bold"></use></svg>
							<svg class="icon minus" focusable="false"><use xlink:href="#minus-bold" href="#minus-bold"></use></svg>
						</span>
					</a>
				</h3>
				<div class="su12-accordion-faqs__contents" id="anchor-id218">
					<div class="su12-accordion-faqs__contents-description">Galaxy smartphones have always offered expansive, cinematic displays with their minimal bezels, wide aspect ratios and innovative display technology. 
<br />
<br />• Galaxy S26 Ultra features the largest display amongst the Galaxy S Series. Galaxy S26 Ultra's display is 6.9-inches corner to corner, with a cinematic 19.5:9 screen ratio.<sup>42</sup>
<br />
<br />• Galaxy Z Fold7's main screen is 8.0-inches corner to corner which offers an expansive display that then folds to be portable.<sup>43</sup>
<br />
<br />• Both Galaxy S26 Ultra's display as well as Galaxy Z Fold7's main screen reach refresh rates up to 120 Hz with peak brightness of up to 2600 nits. </div>
					
					
						
					<!--
						<div class="su12-accordion-faqs__contents-disclaimer-wrap">
							<p class="su12-accordion-faqs__contents-disclaimer">...omitted...</p>
						</div>-->
						
					

					
				</div>
			</li>
		
			
			
			<li class="su12-accordion-faqs__item " an-tr="su12_accordion faqs-product family showcase-cta-content_click" an-ca="content click" an-ac="feature" an-la="faq:accordion:whats the best galaxy smartphone suitable for high end gaming" role="listitem">
				<h3>
					<a href="javascript:void(0)" class="su12-accordion-faqs__title" aria-expanded="false" role="button">
						
						<div class="su12-accordion-faqs__title-text">What&#39;s the best Galaxy smartphone suitable for high-end gaming?</div>
						<span class="icon-wrap">
							<svg class="icon plus" focusable="false"><use xlink:href="#plus-bold" href="#plus-bold"></use></svg>
							<svg class="icon minus" focusable="false"><use xlink:href="#minus-bold" href="#minus-bold"></use></svg>
						</span>
					</a>
				</h3>
				<div class="su12-accordion-faqs__contents" id="anchor-id376">
					<div class="su12-accordion-faqs__contents-description">With powerful processors enabling ray tracing performance, innovative Vapor Chamber cooling systems, Vulkan optimization and long-lasting batteries, the gaming experience on Galaxy smartphones is unbeatable — especially on Galaxy S26 Ultra.<sup>9</sup>
<br />
<br />• Galaxy S26 Ultra features the next-gen custom AP, Snapdragon® 8 Elite Gen 5 for Galaxy, and a reconfigured Vapor Chamber for a 21% performance improvement, enabling smooth, fast and cool gameplay.<sup>6,7,8</sup>
<br />
<br />• Galaxy Z Fold7's 8-inch main screen unfolds to immerse you in the action with vibrant colors and detailed clarity.<sup>43</sup></div>
					
					
						
					<!--
						<div class="su12-accordion-faqs__contents-disclaimer-wrap">
							<p class="su12-accordion-faqs__contents-disclaimer">...omitted...</p>
						</div>-->
						
					

					
				</div>
			</li>
		
			
			
			<li class="su12-accordion-faqs__item " an-tr="su12_accordion faqs-product family showcase-cta-content_click" an-ca="content click" an-ac="feature" an-la="faq:accordion:how good are galaxy smartphones for multitasking" role="listitem">
				<h3>
					<a href="javascript:void(0)" class="su12-accordion-faqs__title" aria-expanded="false" role="button">
						
						<div class="su12-accordion-faqs__title-text">How good are Galaxy smartphones for multitasking?</div>
						<span class="icon-wrap">
							<svg class="icon plus" focusable="false"><use xlink:href="#plus-bold" href="#plus-bold"></use></svg>
							<svg class="icon minus" focusable="false"><use xlink:href="#minus-bold" href="#minus-bold"></use></svg>
						</span>
					</a>
				</h3>
				<div class="su12-accordion-faqs__contents" id="anchor-id471">
					<div class="su12-accordion-faqs__contents-description">Galaxy smartphones are made with multitasking in mind, and both Galaxy S26 Ultra and Galaxy Z Fold7 are powerful enough to withstand busy workdays.
<br />
<br />• Galaxy Z Fold7's 8-inch main screen gives you ample space for multitasking. One UI 8 makes the most of the expansive screen with larger menus and the ability to open multiple windows at once, dragging and dropping between them with ease.<sup>43</sup>
<br />
<br />• Galaxy S26 Ultra delivers Ultra-level performance that makes productivity feel fast and easy. And Galaxy S26 Ultra also comes with S Pen built in. Pop it out to take notes, sketch and even make searching for info feel simpler.
<br />
<br />• With new Galaxy AI features, like Now Nudge and Search, you can just tap or ask to get things done more efficiently.<sup>44</sup></div>
					
					
						
					<!--
						<div class="su12-accordion-faqs__contents-disclaimer-wrap">
							<p class="su12-accordion-faqs__contents-disclaimer">...omitted...</p>
						</div>-->
						
					

					
				</div>
			</li>
		
			
			
			<li class="su12-accordion-faqs__item " an-tr="su12_accordion faqs-product family showcase-cta-content_click" an-ca="content click" an-ac="feature" an-la="faq:accordion:which galaxy smartphone has the best camera" role="listitem">
				<h3>
					<a href="javascript:void(0)" class="su12-accordion-faqs__title" aria-expanded="false" role="button">
						
						<div class="su12-accordion-faqs__title-text">Which Galaxy smartphone has the best camera?</div>
						<span class="icon-wrap">
							<svg class="icon plus" focusable="false"><use xlink:href="#plus-bold" href="#plus-bold"></use></svg>
							<svg class="icon minus" focusable="false"><use xlink:href="#minus-bold" href="#minus-bold"></use></svg>
						</span>
					</a>
				</h3>
				<div class="su12-accordion-faqs__contents" id="anchor-id584">
					<div class="su12-accordion-faqs__contents-description">Each camera in the Galaxy lineup is powerful, but Galaxy S26 Ultra and Galaxy Z Fold7 have some of Galaxy's best-performing cameras, including a 200 MP Wide camera that delivers clear photos even in low light.<sup>12,15</sup>
<br />
<br />• You can capture effortless, high-quality photos with Galaxy cameras and the ProVisual Engine. The ProVisual Engine detects subjects and lighting, optimizing every capture for improved details, skin tone precision, true-to-life colors and improved low-light results.<sup>2</sup>
<br />
<br />• Galaxy S26 Ultra camera also captures clear photos from further away with 100x Space Zoom. Dual telephoto lenses harness 3x and 5x optical zoom plus 2x, 10x optical quality zoom to provide sharper and more detailed shots.<sup>13,17</sup>
<br />
<br />• When shooting video on Galaxy S26 Ultra, it’s easy to capture vivid, detailed and stable footage even at night. Wider apertures on the camera clear up the scene by pulling in more light.<sup>11</sup>
<br />
<br />• The new Super Steady with Horizontal Lock feature helps ensure action shots are clear and steady with upgraded stabilization functions.<sup>18</sup></div>
					
					
						
					<!--
						<div class="su12-accordion-faqs__contents-disclaimer-wrap">
							<p class="su12-accordion-faqs__contents-disclaimer">...omitted...</p>
						</div>-->
						
					

					
				</div>
			</li>
		
			
			
			<li class="su12-accordion-faqs__item " an-tr="su12_accordion faqs-product family showcase-cta-content_click" an-ca="content click" an-ac="feature" an-la="faq:accordion:what is nightography and which galaxy phones take good night videos" role="listitem">
				<h3>
					<a href="javascript:void(0)" class="su12-accordion-faqs__title" aria-expanded="false" role="button">
						
						<div class="su12-accordion-faqs__title-text">What is Nightography and which Galaxy phones take good night videos?</div>
						<span class="icon-wrap">
							<svg class="icon plus" focusable="false"><use xlink:href="#plus-bold" href="#plus-bold"></use></svg>
							<svg class="icon minus" focusable="false"><use xlink:href="#minus-bold" href="#minus-bold"></use></svg>
						</span>
					</a>
				</h3>
				<div class="su12-accordion-faqs__contents" id="anchor-id673">
					<div class="su12-accordion-faqs__contents-description">Nightography is the name of our signature low-light camera functions, the combination of advanced AP and ProVisual Engine that delivers detail and clarity in low-light settings.<sup>11,15</sup>
<br />
<br />• Both professional and casual users will love the easier low-light shooting. The aperture on Galaxy S26 Ultra's Wide camera is 47% brighter to pull in more light, ideal for balanced, well-lit videos in low light.<sup>14</sup>
<br />
<br />• The advanced processor enhances the low-light video performance even further by enabling Nightography. It detects the characteristics of each camera's sensor and delivers optimized noise reduction.
<br />
<br />• When taking photos, the camera intelligently combines multiple exposures, automatically taken when you tap the shutter button. These exposures are then synthesized to fill in missing details and lighten up dark areas.</div>
					
					
						
					<!--
						<div class="su12-accordion-faqs__contents-disclaimer-wrap">
							<p class="su12-accordion-faqs__contents-disclaimer">...omitted...</p>
						</div>-->
						
					

					
				</div>
			</li>
		
			
			
			<li class="su12-accordion-faqs__item " an-tr="su12_accordion faqs-product family showcase-cta-content_click" an-ca="content click" an-ac="feature" an-la="faq:accordion:which zoom options does the samsung galaxy have" role="listitem">
				<h3>
					<a href="javascript:void(0)" class="su12-accordion-faqs__title" aria-expanded="false" role="button">
						
						<div class="su12-accordion-faqs__title-text">Which zoom options does the Samsung Galaxy have? </div>
						<span class="icon-wrap">
							<svg class="icon plus" focusable="false"><use xlink:href="#plus-bold" href="#plus-bold"></use></svg>
							<svg class="icon minus" focusable="false"><use xlink:href="#minus-bold" href="#minus-bold"></use></svg>
						</span>
					</a>
				</h3>
				<div class="su12-accordion-faqs__contents" id="anchor-id761">
					<div class="su12-accordion-faqs__contents-description">The cameras on Galaxy all offer clear zoom capabilities but the best possible zoom options on a Samsung Galaxy smartphone currently can be found on Galaxy S26 Ultra, with its 100x Space Zoom.
<br />
<br />• The powerful camera system on Galaxy S26 Ultra comes with 3x and 5x optical zoom as well as 2x and 10x optical quality zoom. It can then zoom up to 100x digital Space Zoom. The 50 MP Telephoto camera, which has 5x optical zoom and 10x optical quality zoom, also features an F2.9 aperture that is 37% brighter than Galaxy S25 Ultra.<sup>15,17</sup>
<br />
<br />• Galaxy S26+ and Galaxy S26, as well as Galaxy Z Fold7, have up to 30x digital zoom, with 3x optical zoom and 2x optical quality zoom.
<br />
<br />• Galaxy Z Flip7 has up to 10x digital zoom, with 2x optical quality zoom.</div>
					
					
						
					<!--
						<div class="su12-accordion-faqs__contents-disclaimer-wrap">
							<p class="su12-accordion-faqs__contents-disclaimer">...omitted...</p>
						</div>-->
						
					

					
				</div>
			</li>
		
			
			
			<li class="su12-accordion-faqs__item " an-tr="su12_accordion faqs-product family showcase-cta-content_click" an-ca="content click" an-ac="feature" an-la="faq:accordion:why are samsung phones the best for selfies" role="listitem">
				<h3>
					<a href="javascript:void(0)" class="su12-accordion-faqs__title" aria-expanded="false" role="button">
						
						<div class="su12-accordion-faqs__title-text">Why are Samsung phones the best for selfies?</div>
						<span class="icon-wrap">
							<svg class="icon plus" focusable="false"><use xlink:href="#plus-bold" href="#plus-bold"></use></svg>
							<svg class="icon minus" focusable="false"><use xlink:href="#minus-bold" href="#minus-bold"></use></svg>
						</span>
					</a>
				</h3>
				<div class="su12-accordion-faqs__contents" id="anchor-id866">
					<div class="su12-accordion-faqs__contents-description">If you love taking selfies, the camera on a Galaxy smartphone is your best bet — and there are a few great options to choose from.
<br />
<br />• Galaxy cameras include innovative technology like the ProVisual Engine optimizing every capture for improved details, skin tone precision, true-to-life colors and improved low-light results.<sup>15</sup>
<br />
<br />• AI ISP (Image Signal Processor) has been added to the front camera on the Galaxy S26 Series to provide natural-looking selfies.
<br />
<br />• With its unique form factor, Galaxy Z Flip7 allows you to take high-resolution selfies. The 50 MP Wide camera can be easily accessed when the phone is folded, using the cover screen to help you shoot.<sup>45</sup></div>
					
					
						
					<!--
						<div class="su12-accordion-faqs__contents-disclaimer-wrap">
							<p class="su12-accordion-faqs__contents-disclaimer">...omitted...</p>
						</div>-->
						
					

					
				</div>
			</li>
		
			
			
			<li class="su12-accordion-faqs__item " an-tr="su12_accordion faqs-product family showcase-cta-content_click" an-ca="content click" an-ac="feature" an-la="faq:accordion:how long does a galaxy battery last in a day" role="listitem">
				<h3>
					<a href="javascript:void(0)" class="su12-accordion-faqs__title" aria-expanded="false" role="button">
						
						<div class="su12-accordion-faqs__title-text">How long does a Galaxy battery last in a day?</div>
						<span class="icon-wrap">
							<svg class="icon plus" focusable="false"><use xlink:href="#plus-bold" href="#plus-bold"></use></svg>
							<svg class="icon minus" focusable="false"><use xlink:href="#minus-bold" href="#minus-bold"></use></svg>
						</span>
					</a>
				</h3>
				<div class="su12-accordion-faqs__contents" id="anchor-id947">
					<div class="su12-accordion-faqs__contents-description">With their high-capacity batteries and hardware and software innovation that helps enhance battery life, our flagship Galaxy phones all offer many hours of use before you need to charge.
<br />
<br />• Galaxy S26 Ultra has 5000 mAh and provides up to 31 hours of video playback time.
<br />
<br />• Galaxy S26+ has 4900 mAh for up to 31 hours of video playback time.
<br />
<br />• Galaxy S26 has 4300 mAh to give users up to 30 hours of video playback time.
<br />
<br />• Galaxy Z Fold7's 4400 mAh battery provides up to 24 hours of video playback time.
<br />
<br />• Galaxy Z Flip7 offers 4300 mAh and up to 31 hours of video playback time.<sup>22,23,46,47,48</sup></div>
					
					
						
					<!--
						<div class="su12-accordion-faqs__contents-disclaimer-wrap">
							<p class="su12-accordion-faqs__contents-disclaimer">...omitted...</p>
						</div>-->
						
					

					
				</div>
			</li>
		
			
			
			<li class="su12-accordion-faqs__item " an-tr="su12_accordion faqs-product family showcase-cta-content_click" an-ca="content click" an-ac="feature" an-la="faq:accordion:how long does it take to fully charge galaxy smartphones" role="listitem">
				<h3>
					<a href="javascript:void(0)" class="su12-accordion-faqs__title" aria-expanded="false" role="button">
						
						<div class="su12-accordion-faqs__title-text">How long does it take to fully charge Galaxy smartphones?</div>
						<span class="icon-wrap">
							<svg class="icon plus" focusable="false"><use xlink:href="#plus-bold" href="#plus-bold"></use></svg>
							<svg class="icon minus" focusable="false"><use xlink:href="#minus-bold" href="#minus-bold"></use></svg>
						</span>
					</a>
				</h3>
				<div class="su12-accordion-faqs__contents" id="anchor-id1074">
					<div class="su12-accordion-faqs__contents-description">Galaxy's flagship smartphones have incredibly long battery life, and with the addition of Super Fast Charging, you can recharge fast.
<br />
<br />• Galaxy S26 Ultra has the largest battery capacity on a Galaxy S Series smartphone with 5000 mAh, while Galaxy S26+ has 4900 mAh and Galaxy S26 has 4300 mAh. Galaxy Z Fold7 has 4400 mAh, while Galaxy Z Flip7 offers 4300 mAh.<sup>23,48</sup>
<br />
<br />• Wired Super Fast Charging 3.0 lets you charge the battery on your Galaxy S26 Ultra up to 75% in around 30 minutes. </div>
					
					
						
					<!--
						<div class="su12-accordion-faqs__contents-disclaimer-wrap">
							<p class="su12-accordion-faqs__contents-disclaimer">...omitted...</p>
						</div>-->
						
					

					
				</div>
			</li>
		
			
			
			<li class="su12-accordion-faqs__item " an-tr="su12_accordion faqs-product family showcase-cta-content_click" an-ca="content click" an-ac="feature" an-la="faq:accordion:what is the dual rail hinge in a samsung phone and what is it for" role="listitem">
				<h3>
					<a href="javascript:void(0)" class="su12-accordion-faqs__title" aria-expanded="false" role="button">
						
						<div class="su12-accordion-faqs__title-text">What is the dual-rail hinge in a Samsung phone and what is it for? </div>
						<span class="icon-wrap">
							<svg class="icon plus" focusable="false"><use xlink:href="#plus-bold" href="#plus-bold"></use></svg>
							<svg class="icon minus" focusable="false"><use xlink:href="#minus-bold" href="#minus-bold"></use></svg>
						</span>
					</a>
				</h3>
				<div class="su12-accordion-faqs__contents" id="anchor-id1128">
					<div class="su12-accordion-faqs__contents-description">The dual-rail hinge, which is part of the Armor FlexHinge, is an innovative evolution of the hinge that supports our slim Galaxy Foldables.<sup>29,30</sup>
<br />
<br />• Armor FlexHinge was first introduced on Galaxy Z Fold7, enabling a thickness of just 8.9 mm when folded and setting a new standard for slim foldables.<sup>26</sup>
<br />
<br />• Armor FlexHinge is also found on Galaxy Z Flip7, which measures just 13.7 mm thick when folded.<sup>26</sup>
<br />
<br />• With an enhanced water droplet design and newly implemented multi-rail structure, Armor FlexHinge helps reduce visible creasing and strengthen durability by evenly dispersing stress.</div>
					
					
						
					<!--
						<div class="su12-accordion-faqs__contents-disclaimer-wrap">
							<p class="su12-accordion-faqs__contents-disclaimer">...omitted...</p>
						</div>-->
						
					

					
				</div>
			</li>
		
			
			
			<li class="su12-accordion-faqs__item " an-tr="su12_accordion faqs-product family showcase-cta-content_click" an-ca="content click" an-ac="feature" an-la="faq:accordion:how durable are galaxy phones" role="listitem">
				<h3>
					<a href="javascript:void(0)" class="su12-accordion-faqs__title" aria-expanded="false" role="button">
						
						<div class="su12-accordion-faqs__title-text">How durable are Galaxy phones?</div>
						<span class="icon-wrap">
							<svg class="icon plus" focusable="false"><use xlink:href="#plus-bold" href="#plus-bold"></use></svg>
							<svg class="icon minus" focusable="false"><use xlink:href="#minus-bold" href="#minus-bold"></use></svg>
						</span>
					</a>
				</h3>
				<div class="su12-accordion-faqs__contents" id="anchor-id1240">
					<div class="su12-accordion-faqs__contents-description">Thanks to the neverending pursuit of innovation and engineering, Galaxy smartphones, including Galaxy S26 Ultra, are built to be slim yet strong with durable materials.
<br />
<br />• The latest Galaxy smartphones feature displays protected with revolutionary Corning® display glass, delivering durability and clarity. Galaxy S26 Ultra comes with Corning® Gorilla® Armor 2 on the display for scratch-resistant views, and the back glass is also protected with clear and tough Corning® Gorilla® Glass Victus® 2, allowing the unique color to shine.
<br />
<br />• The frame is made of lightweight and strong Armor Aluminum.<sup>27</sup>
<br />
<br />• The Galaxy S26 Series all have an IP68 rating, meaning they're water and dust resistant.<sup>49</sup></div>
					
					
						
					<!--
						<div class="su12-accordion-faqs__contents-disclaimer-wrap">
							<p class="su12-accordion-faqs__contents-disclaimer">...omitted...</p>
						</div>-->
						
					

					
				</div>
			</li>
		
			
			
			<li class="su12-accordion-faqs__item " an-tr="su12_accordion faqs-product family showcase-cta-content_click" an-ca="content click" an-ac="feature" an-la="faq:accordion:what are the benefits of a cover screen" role="listitem">
				<h3>
					<a href="javascript:void(0)" class="su12-accordion-faqs__title" aria-expanded="false" role="button">
						
						<div class="su12-accordion-faqs__title-text">What are the benefits of a cover screen?</div>
						<span class="icon-wrap">
							<svg class="icon plus" focusable="false"><use xlink:href="#plus-bold" href="#plus-bold"></use></svg>
							<svg class="icon minus" focusable="false"><use xlink:href="#minus-bold" href="#minus-bold"></use></svg>
						</span>
					</a>
				</h3>
				<div class="su12-accordion-faqs__contents" id="anchor-id1358">
					<div class="su12-accordion-faqs__contents-description">Available only on Galaxy Foldables, the cover screens on Galaxy Z Fold7 and Galaxy Z Flip7 give users a convenient experience without unfolding.
<br />
<br />• Galaxy Z Fold7's 6.5-inch cover screen has been expanded for a 21:9 ratio to provide the experience of a standard premium smartphone that you can use comfortably before unfolding to use the larger main screen. Shoot and edit content, type naturally and even use AI to get things done with ease.<sup>50</sup>
<br />
<br />• Galaxy Z Flip7's 4.1-inch cover screen is also called the FlexWindow. It has the slimmest bezel on a Flip device yet to give users more space to work with before unfolding. Use it to capture your 50 MP selfies, access Now Brief and Now Bar or ask AI for information through the camera.<sup>33</sup>
<br />
<br />• One UI 8, made specially for Galaxy Foldables, let you personalize your cover screens with custom wallpapers and widgets.<sup>51</sup></div>
					
					
						
					<!--
						<div class="su12-accordion-faqs__contents-disclaimer-wrap">
							<p class="su12-accordion-faqs__contents-disclaimer">...omitted...</p>
						</div>-->
						
					

					
				</div>
			</li>
		
			
			
			<li class="su12-accordion-faqs__item " an-tr="su12_accordion faqs-product family showcase-cta-content_click" an-ca="content click" an-ac="feature" an-la="faq:accordion:what are the key features of samsung galaxy s26 series smartphones" role="listitem">
				<h3>
					<a href="javascript:void(0)" class="su12-accordion-faqs__title" aria-expanded="false" role="button">
						
						<div class="su12-accordion-faqs__title-text">What are the key features of Samsung Galaxy S26 Series smartphones?</div>
						<span class="icon-wrap">
							<svg class="icon plus" focusable="false"><use xlink:href="#plus-bold" href="#plus-bold"></use></svg>
							<svg class="icon minus" focusable="false"><use xlink:href="#minus-bold" href="#minus-bold"></use></svg>
						</span>
					</a>
				</h3>
				<div class="su12-accordion-faqs__contents" id="anchor-id1445">
					<div class="su12-accordion-faqs__contents-description">The new Galaxy S26 Series smartphones stand out from with premium design, powerful performance and easy-to-use AI features.
<br />
<br />• The sleek, durable design across all three models offer a slim, refined build that is engineered to last. The hardware innovation combines expansive anti-reflective displays with refined Armor Aluminum frames that include rounded, ergonomic corners.<sup>27</sup>
<br />
<br />• Galaxy S26 Ultra's 200 MP camera system and improved f-stops offer clear pictures even at night.
<br />
<br />• Galaxy S26 and Galaxy S26+ feature a 50 MP Wide camera to capture your life, day or night, as well as a powerful chipset for fast tasking, enabling them to seamlessly fit into your daily routine.
<br />
<br />• Galaxy S26 Ultra comes equipped with an exclusive Snapdragon® 8 Elite Gen 5 processor that is customized for Galaxy with improved NPU, GPU and CPU for smoother graphics.<sup>6,7</sup>
<br />
<br />• With the world's first Privacy Display on a mobile, Galaxy S26 Ultra's screen provides added privacy when you’re out in public ensuring your personal details remain safe.<sup>1</sup>
<br />
<br />• The whole Galaxy S26 Series comes with deep AI integration that goes well beyond your typical smartphone. From instant cross-app tasks and smart photo editing to real-time translation and easy-to-use productivity tools that are intuitive and efficient for everyday use.</div>
					
					
						
					<!--
						<div class="su12-accordion-faqs__contents-disclaimer-wrap">
							<p class="su12-accordion-faqs__contents-disclaimer">...omitted...</p>
						</div>-->
						
					

					
				</div>
			</li>
		
			
			
			<li class="su12-accordion-faqs__item " an-tr="su12_accordion faqs-product family showcase-cta-content_click" an-ca="content click" an-ac="feature" an-la="faq:accordion:what are the benefits of using a galaxy watch with a samsung phone" role="listitem">
				<h3>
					<a href="javascript:void(0)" class="su12-accordion-faqs__title" aria-expanded="false" role="button">
						
						<div class="su12-accordion-faqs__title-text">What are the benefits of using a Galaxy Watch with a Samsung phone?</div>
						<span class="icon-wrap">
							<svg class="icon plus" focusable="false"><use xlink:href="#plus-bold" href="#plus-bold"></use></svg>
							<svg class="icon minus" focusable="false"><use xlink:href="#minus-bold" href="#minus-bold"></use></svg>
						</span>
					</a>
				</h3>
				<div class="su12-accordion-faqs__contents" id="anchor-id1555">
					<div class="su12-accordion-faqs__contents-description">Keeping track of your wellness goals on the Samsung Health app is simple with the Galaxy ecosystem, including devices like Galaxy S26 Ultra and Galaxy Watches.<sup>36,38,52</sup>
<br />
<br />• When paired with Galaxy S26 Ultra, Galaxy Watch gets to know your body and your routine, analyzing your sleep and workouts to create personalized plans, with comprehensive analytics and suggestions to help ensure you feel your best all day, every day.
<br />
<br />• The Samsung Health app on Galaxy S26 Ultra delivers in-depth insights for things like sleep, exercise, nutrition, heart health and more. </div>
					
					
						
					<!--
						<div class="su12-accordion-faqs__contents-disclaimer-wrap">
							<p class="su12-accordion-faqs__contents-disclaimer">...omitted...</p>
						</div>-->
						
					

					
				</div>
			</li>
		
	</ul>
</div>

  <script type="application/ld+json" data-type="seo" data-object-type="FAQPage" data-id="486ee6d0-b8ef-4db7-9779-5f5cd9d7f0d3">{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"FAQPage","@id":"https://www.samsung.com/pk/mobile/#FAQ","mainEntity":[{"@type":"Question","name":"What are the newest and latest Samsung mobile products?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"During the latest Unpacked on February 25, 2026, Samsung was pleased to release a wide range of innovative new products including the Galaxy S26 Series and new Galaxy Buds. \r\n<br>\r\n<br>• The newest S Series smartphones are Galaxy S26 Ultra, Galaxy S26+ and Galaxy S26, which combine slim design with next-gen performance and convenient AI assistance. You can maximize your Galaxy experience with the Galaxy Buds4 Pro and Galaxy Buds4, featuring a reimagined blade design and clear delivery of Hi-Fi sound.\r\n<br>\r\n<br>• Enhance your productivity and daily life with the latest Galaxy Watch models, the Galaxy Watch8 series, which includes Galaxy Watch8, Galaxy Watch8 Classic and Galaxy Watch8 Ultra, providing AI support and wellness tracking right from your wrist."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What is Privacy Display and how can I use it?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"The world's first smartphone Privacy Display is a built-in privacy screen on Galaxy S26 Ultra that uses innovative technology to protect your device's display from prying eyes in public places.\r\n<br><br>• When activated, the screen's pixels move dynamically to protect your private information by obscuring what's on your screen from view.\r\n<br><br>• Choose to have the full screen hidden at all times or customize further and have it activate when selected apps are in use or when you receive certain notifications that you want to keep private.<sup>1</sup>"}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Which Galaxy smartphones have big displays?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Galaxy smartphones have always offered expansive, cinematic displays with their minimal bezels, wide aspect ratios and innovative display technology. \r\n<br>\r\n<br>• Galaxy S26 Ultra features the largest display amongst the Galaxy S Series. Galaxy S26 Ultra's display is 6.9-inches corner to corner, with a cinematic 19.5:9 screen ratio.<sup>42</sup>\r\n<br>\r\n<br>• Galaxy Z Fold7's main screen is 8.0-inches corner to corner which offers an expansive display that then folds to be portable.<sup>43</sup>\r\n<br>\r\n<br>• Both Galaxy S26 Ultra's display as well as Galaxy Z Fold7's main screen reach refresh rates up to 120 Hz with peak brightness of up to 2600 nits. "}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What's the best Galaxy smartphone suitable for high-end gaming?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"With powerful processors enabling ray tracing performance, innovative Vapor Chamber cooling systems, Vulkan optimization and long-lasting batteries, the gaming experience on Galaxy smartphones is unbeatable — especially on Galaxy S26 Ultra.<sup>9</sup>\r\n<br>\r\n<br>• Galaxy S26 Ultra features the next-gen custom AP, Snapdragon® 8 Elite Gen 5 for Galaxy, and a reconfigured Vapor Chamber for a 21% performance improvement, enabling smooth, fast and cool gameplay.<sup>6,7,8</sup>\r\n<br>\r\n<br>• Galaxy Z Fold7's 8-inch main screen unfolds to immerse you in the action with vibrant colors and detailed clarity.<sup>43</sup>"}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How good are Galaxy smartphones for multitasking?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Galaxy smartphones are made with multitasking in mind, and both Galaxy S26 Ultra and Galaxy Z Fold7 are powerful enough to withstand busy workdays.\r\n<br>\r\n<br>• Galaxy Z Fold7's 8-inch main screen gives you ample space for multitasking. One UI 8 makes the most of the expansive screen with larger menus and the ability to open multiple windows at once, dragging and dropping between them with ease.<sup>43</sup>\r\n<br>\r\n<br>• Galaxy S26 Ultra delivers Ultra-level performance that makes productivity feel fast and easy. And Galaxy S26 Ultra also comes with S Pen built in. Pop it out to take notes, sketch and even make searching for info feel simpler.\r\n<br>\r\n<br>• With new Galaxy AI features, like Now Nudge and Search, you can just tap or ask to get things done more efficiently.<sup>44</sup>"}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Which Galaxy smartphone has the best camera?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Each camera in the Galaxy lineup is powerful, but Galaxy S26 Ultra and Galaxy Z Fold7 have some of Galaxy's best-performing cameras, including a 200 MP Wide camera that delivers clear photos even in low light.<sup>12,15</sup>\r\n<br>\r\n<br>• You can capture effortless, high-quality photos with Galaxy cameras and the ProVisual Engine. The ProVisual Engine detects subjects and lighting, optimizing every capture for improved details, skin tone precision, true-to-life colors and improved low-light results.<sup>2</sup>\r\n<br>\r\n<br>• Galaxy S26 Ultra camera also captures clear photos from further away with 100x Space Zoom. Dual telephoto lenses harness 3x and 5x optical zoom plus 2x, 10x optical quality zoom to provide sharper and more detailed shots.<sup>13,17</sup>\r\n<br>\r\n<br>• When shooting video on Galaxy S26 Ultra, it’s easy to capture vivid, detailed and stable footage even at night. Wider apertures on the camera clear up the scene by pulling in more light.<sup>11</sup>\r\n<br>\r\n<br>• The new Super Steady with Horizontal Lock feature helps ensure action shots are clear and steady with upgraded stabilization functions.<sup>18</sup>"}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What is Nightography and which Galaxy phones take good night videos?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Nightography is the name of our signature low-light camera functions, the combination of advanced AP and ProVisual Engine that delivers detail and clarity in low-light settings.<sup>11,15</sup>\r\n<br>\r\n<br>• Both professional and casual users will love the easier low-light shooting. The aperture on Galaxy S26 Ultra's Wide camera is 47% brighter to pull in more light, ideal for balanced, well-lit videos in low light.<sup>14</sup>\r\n<br>\r\n<br>• The advanced processor enhances the low-light video performance even further by enabling Nightography. It detects the characteristics of each camera's sensor and delivers optimized noise reduction.\r\n<br>\r\n<br>• When taking photos, the camera intelligently combines multiple exposures, automatically taken when you tap the shutter button. These exposures are then synthesized to fill in missing details and lighten up dark areas."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Which zoom options does the Samsung Galaxy have? ","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"The cameras on Galaxy all offer clear zoom capabilities but the best possible zoom options on a Samsung Galaxy smartphone currently can be found on Galaxy S26 Ultra, with its 100x Space Zoom.\r\n<br>\r\n<br>• The powerful camera system on Galaxy S26 Ultra comes with 3x and 5x optical zoom as well as 2x and 10x optical quality zoom. It can then zoom up to 100x digital Space Zoom. The 50 MP Telephoto camera, which has 5x optical zoom and 10x optical quality zoom, also features an F2.9 aperture that is 37% brighter than Galaxy S25 Ultra.<sup>15,17</sup>\r\n<br>\r\n<br>• Galaxy S26+ and Galaxy S26, as well as Galaxy Z Fold7, have up to 30x digital zoom, with 3x optical zoom and 2x optical quality zoom.\r\n<br>\r\n<br>• Galaxy Z Flip7 has up to 10x digital zoom, with 2x optical quality zoom."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Why are Samsung phones the best for selfies?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"If you love taking selfies, the camera on a Galaxy smartphone is your best bet — and there are a few great options to choose from.\r\n<br>\r\n<br>• Galaxy cameras include innovative technology like the ProVisual Engine optimizing every capture for improved details, skin tone precision, true-to-life colors and improved low-light results.<sup>15</sup>\r\n<br>\r\n<br>• AI ISP (Image Signal Processor) has been added to the front camera on the Galaxy S26 Series to provide natural-looking selfies.\r\n<br>\r\n<br>• With its unique form factor, Galaxy Z Flip7 allows you to take high-resolution selfies. The 50 MP Wide camera can be easily accessed when the phone is folded, using the cover screen to help you shoot.<sup>45</sup>"}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How long does a Galaxy battery last in a day?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"With their high-capacity batteries and hardware and software innovation that helps enhance battery life, our flagship Galaxy phones all offer many hours of use before you need to charge.\r\n<br>\r\n<br>• Galaxy S26 Ultra has 5000 mAh and provides up to 31 hours of video playback time.\r\n<br>\r\n<br>• Galaxy S26+ has 4900 mAh for up to 31 hours of video playback time.\r\n<br>\r\n<br>• Galaxy S26 has 4300 mAh to give users up to 30 hours of video playback time.\r\n<br>\r\n<br>• Galaxy Z Fold7's 4400 mAh battery provides up to 24 hours of video playback time.\r\n<br>\r\n<br>• Galaxy Z Flip7 offers 4300 mAh and up to 31 hours of video playback time.<sup>22,23,46,47,48</sup>"}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How long does it take to fully charge Galaxy smartphones?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Galaxy's flagship smartphones have incredibly long battery life, and with the addition of Super Fast Charging, you can recharge fast.\r\n<br>\r\n<br>• Galaxy S26 Ultra has the largest battery capacity on a Galaxy S Series smartphone with 5000 mAh, while Galaxy S26+ has 4900 mAh and Galaxy S26 has 4300 mAh. Galaxy Z Fold7 has 4400 mAh, while Galaxy Z Flip7 offers 4300 mAh.<sup>23,48</sup>\r\n<br>\r\n<br>• Wired Super Fast Charging 3.0 lets you charge the battery on your Galaxy S26 Ultra up to 75% in around 30 minutes. "}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What is the dual-rail hinge in a Samsung phone and what is it for? ","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"The dual-rail hinge, which is part of the Armor FlexHinge, is an innovative evolution of the hinge that supports our slim Galaxy Foldables.<sup>29,30</sup>\r\n<br>\r\n<br>• Armor FlexHinge was first introduced on Galaxy Z Fold7, enabling a thickness of just 8.9 mm when folded and setting a new standard for slim foldables.<sup>26</sup>\r\n<br>\r\n<br>• Armor FlexHinge is also found on Galaxy Z Flip7, which measures just 13.7 mm thick when folded.<sup>26</sup>\r\n<br>\r\n<br>• With an enhanced water droplet design and newly implemented multi-rail structure, Armor FlexHinge helps reduce visible creasing and strengthen durability by evenly dispersing stress."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How durable are Galaxy phones?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Thanks to the neverending pursuit of innovation and engineering, Galaxy smartphones, including Galaxy S26 Ultra, are built to be slim yet strong with durable materials.\r\n<br>\r\n<br>• The latest Galaxy smartphones feature displays protected with revolutionary Corning® display glass, delivering durability and clarity. Galaxy S26 Ultra comes with Corning® Gorilla® Armor 2 on the display for scratch-resistant views, and the back glass is also protected with clear and tough Corning® Gorilla® Glass Victus® 2, allowing the unique color to shine.\r\n<br>\r\n<br>• The frame is made of lightweight and strong Armor Aluminum.<sup>27</sup>\r\n<br>\r\n<br>• The Galaxy S26 Series all have an IP68 rating, meaning they're water and dust resistant.<sup>49</sup>"}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What are the benefits of a cover screen?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Available only on Galaxy Foldables, the cover screens on Galaxy Z Fold7 and Galaxy Z Flip7 give users a convenient experience without unfolding.\r\n<br>\r\n<br>• Galaxy Z Fold7's 6.5-inch cover screen has been expanded for a 21:9 ratio to provide the experience of a standard premium smartphone that you can use comfortably before unfolding to use the larger main screen. Shoot and edit content, type naturally and even use AI to get things done with ease.<sup>50</sup>\r\n<br>\r\n<br>• Galaxy Z Flip7's 4.1-inch cover screen is also called the FlexWindow. It has the slimmest bezel on a Flip device yet to give users more space to work with before unfolding. Use it to capture your 50 MP selfies, access Now Brief and Now Bar or ask AI for information through the camera.<sup>33</sup>\r\n<br>\r\n<br>• One UI 8, made specially for Galaxy Foldables, let you personalize your cover screens with custom wallpapers and widgets.<sup>51</sup>"}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What are the key features of Samsung Galaxy S26 Series smartphones?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"The new Galaxy S26 Series smartphones stand out from with premium design, powerful performance and easy-to-use AI features.\r\n<br>\r\n<br>• The sleek, durable design across all three models offer a slim, refined build that is engineered to last. The hardware innovation combines expansive anti-reflective displays with refined Armor Aluminum frames that include rounded, ergonomic corners.<sup>27</sup>\r\n<br>\r\n<br>• Galaxy S26 Ultra's 200 MP camera system and improved f-stops offer clear pictures even at night.\r\n<br>\r\n<br>• Galaxy S26 and Galaxy S26+ feature a 50 MP Wide camera to capture your life, day or night, as well as a powerful chipset for fast tasking, enabling them to seamlessly fit into your daily routine.\r\n<br>\r\n<br>• Galaxy S26 Ultra comes equipped with an exclusive Snapdragon® 8 Elite Gen 5 processor that is customized for Galaxy with improved NPU, GPU and CPU for smoother graphics.<sup>6,7</sup>\r\n<br>\r\n<br>• With the world's first Privacy Display on a mobile, Galaxy S26 Ultra's screen provides added privacy when you’re out in public ensuring your personal details remain safe.<sup>1</sup>\r\n<br>\r\n<br>• The whole Galaxy S26 Series comes with deep AI integration that goes well beyond your typical smartphone. From instant cross-app tasks and smart photo editing to real-time translation and easy-to-use productivity tools that are intuitive and efficient for everyday use."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What are the benefits of using a Galaxy Watch with a Samsung phone?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Keeping track of your wellness goals on the Samsung Health app is simple with the Galaxy ecosystem, including devices like Galaxy S26 Ultra and Galaxy Watches.<sup>36,38,52</sup>\r\n<br>\r\n<br>• When paired with Galaxy S26 Ultra, Galaxy Watch gets to know your body and your routine, analyzing your sleep and workouts to create personalized plans, with comprehensive analytics and suggestions to help ensure you feel your best all day, every day.\r\n<br>\r\n<br>• The Samsung Health app on Galaxy S26 Ultra delivers in-depth insights for things like sleep, exercise, nutrition, heart health and more. "}}]}</script>


</div>
<div class="cm-g-text-block aem-GridColumn aem-GridColumn--default--12">





  
	<div class="textblock    bg-gray  text-left  text-mo-left container-width-medium">
		
		
    	
    	
    	
    	<div class="textblock__body padding-top--48 padding-bottom--48">
				
				
			
			
			
			
			
			
			
			<div class="textblock__disclaimer">
				
				<ul class="textblock__disclaimer-list" role="list">
            		<li class="textblock__disclaimer-text" role="listitem">*All specifications and descriptions provided herein may be different from the actual specifications and descriptions for the product. Samsung reserves the right to make changes to this document and the product described herein, at any time, without obligation on Samsung to provide notification of such change. All functionality, features, specifications, GUI and other product information provided in this document including, but not limited to, the benefits, design, pricing, components, performance, availability and capabilities of the product are subject to change without notice or obligation. The contents within the screen are simulated images and are for demonstration purposes only.</li>
            	
            		<li class="textblock__disclaimer-text" role="listitem"><br />*Samsung Account login may be required to use certain AI features.</li>
            	
            		<li class="textblock__disclaimer-text" role="listitem"><br />*Samsung does not make any promises, assurances or guarantees as to the accuracy, completeness or reliability of the output provided by AI features.</li>
            	
            		<li class="textblock__disclaimer-text" role="listitem"><br />*Availability of Galaxy AI features may vary depending on the region/country, OS/One UI version, device model and phone carrier.</li>
            	
            		<li class="textblock__disclaimer-text" role="listitem"><br />*Galaxy AI basic features provided by Samsung are free. Future releases may include enhanced features or new services that are offered on a paid basis. Different terms may apply for AI features provided by third parties. Galaxy AI basic features are those services listed under &quot;Advanced intelligence&quot; in the current Samsung Services Terms and Conditions.</li>
            	
            		<li class="textblock__disclaimer-text" role="listitem"><br />*Galaxy AI service may be limited for minors in certain regions with age restrictions over AI usage.</li>
            	
            		<li class="textblock__disclaimer-text" role="listitem"><br />*Device, model and color availability may vary depending on country or carrier. </li>
            	
            		<li class="textblock__disclaimer-text" role="listitem"><br />1. Privacy Display feature controls the screen's viewing angle to limit peripheral vision and can be activated in Settings. Activation for specific apps also available in Settings. Some changes in image quality may occur outside the viewing angle. Some information may still be visible to others depending on the viewing environment, such as angle or brightness. Caution is advised when exposing sensitive information.</li>
            	
            		<li class="textblock__disclaimer-text" role="listitem"><br />2. Compared to previous Galaxy S Series models.</li>
            	
            		<li class="textblock__disclaimer-text" role="listitem"><br />3. ProScaler is supported on Galaxy S26 Ultra and Galaxy S26+ models. Image quality can be enhanced up to QHD+, depending on the screen resolution setting of the device.</li>
            	
            		<li class="textblock__disclaimer-text" role="listitem"><br />4. Results of ProScaler when applied on Galaxy S26 Ultra for illustrative purposes only. Accuracy of results is not guaranteed.</li>
            	
            		<li class="textblock__disclaimer-text" role="listitem"><br />5. On Galaxy S26 Ultra, Corning® Gorilla® Armor 2 is applied to the front of the device and Corning® Gorilla® Glass Victus® 2 is applied to the rear. On Galaxy S26 and Galaxy S26+, Corning® Gorilla® Glass Victus® 2 is applied to both the front and the rear of the device.</li>
            	
            		<li class="textblock__disclaimer-text" role="listitem"><br />6. Snapdragon branded products are products of Qualcomm Technologies, Inc. and/or its subsidiaries. Snapdragon is a trademark or registered trademark of Qualcomm Incorporated.</li>
            	
            		<li class="textblock__disclaimer-text" role="listitem"><br />7. AP performance improvements shown compared to Galaxy S25 Ultra. Actual performance will depend on user environment, conditions and pre-installed software and applications.</li>
            	
            		<li class="textblock__disclaimer-text" role="listitem"><br />8. Vapor Chamber performance improvements shown compared to Galaxy S25 Ultra. Actual performance will depend on user environment, conditions and pre-installed software and applications.</li>
            	
            		<li class="textblock__disclaimer-text" role="listitem"><br />9. Ray tracing and Vulkan is supported on Galaxy S26 devices. Availability may vary by device, content and application.</li>
            	
            		<li class="textblock__disclaimer-text" role="listitem"><br />10. Image(s) simulated for illustrative purposes only. Actual UX/UI may differ.</li>
            	
            		<li class="textblock__disclaimer-text" role="listitem"><br />11. Nightography availability and results may vary by model.</li>
            	
            		<li class="textblock__disclaimer-text" role="listitem"><br />12. 200 MP resolution availability may vary by model.</li>
            	
            		<li class="textblock__disclaimer-text" role="listitem"><br />13. Optical quality zoom is enabled by the Adaptive Pixel sensor. 3x and 5x distances are optical zoom. 2x and 10x distances are optical quality zoom.</li>
            	
            		<li class="textblock__disclaimer-text" role="listitem"><br />14. Brightness improvements shown compared to Galaxy S25 Ultra.</li>
            	
            		<li class="textblock__disclaimer-text" role="listitem"><br />15. Results may vary depending on light condition and/or shooting conditions including multiple subjects, being out of focus or moving subjects.</li>
            	
            		<li class="textblock__disclaimer-text" role="listitem"><br />16. AI Zoom is applied to distances between digital zoom lengths. Accuracy of results is not guaranteed.</li>
            	
            		<li class="textblock__disclaimer-text" role="listitem"><br />17. 100x Space Zoom on Galaxy S26 Ultra includes 10x optical quality zoom and 100x digital zoom with Super Resolution technology. Zoom distances past 10x zoom may express some image deterioration.</li>
            	
            		<li class="textblock__disclaimer-text" role="listitem"><br />18. Super Steady results may vary depending on editing method and/or shooting conditions. </li>
            	
            		<li class="textblock__disclaimer-text" role="listitem"><br />19. Ocean mode is available through Samsung’s Expert RAW App, which can be downloaded from Galaxy Store. Results from ocean mode may vary depending on user settings and/or shooting conditions.</li>
            	
            		<li class="textblock__disclaimer-text" role="listitem"><br />20. Galaxy smartphones used underwater need to be placed in a waterproof underwater housing. Galaxy smartphones are not designed to be waterproof against seawater.</li>
            	
            		<li class="textblock__disclaimer-text" role="listitem"><br />21. Photos were taken entirely using Galaxy S26 Ultra smartphones.</li>
            	
            		<li class="textblock__disclaimer-text" role="listitem"><br />22. Actual battery life varies by network environment, features and apps used, frequency of calls and messages, the number of times charged, and many other factors. Estimated against the average usage profile compiled by UX Connect Research. Independently assessed by UX Connect Research between 2026.1.8-2026.1.30 in US and UK with pre-release versions of SM-S942, SM-S947 and SM-S948 under default setting using LTE and 5G Sub6 networks. NOT tested under 5G mmWave network.</li>
            	
            		<li class="textblock__disclaimer-text" role="listitem"><br />23. Based on Samsung internal lab test conditions with pre-release version of given model connected to earphone via Bluetooth under default settings over LTE. Estimated against battery capacity and measured current over battery power consumption during video playback (video file resolution 720 p, saved on device) on the main screen. Actual video playback time may vary by network connection, settings, video file format, screen brightness, battery condition and many other factors.</li>
            	
            		<li class="textblock__disclaimer-text" role="listitem"><br />24. Typical value tested under third-party laboratory condition. Typical value is the estimated average value considering the deviation in battery capacity among the battery samples tested under IEC 61960 standard. Rated capacity is 4855 mAh for Galaxy S26 Ultra, 4755 mAh for Galaxy S26+ and 4175 mAh for Galaxy S26.</li>
            	
            		<li class="textblock__disclaimer-text" role="listitem"><br />25. A Qi2-compatible case is required to use Super Fast Wireless Charging.</li>
            	
            		<li class="textblock__disclaimer-text" role="listitem"><br />26. Thickness measured from top to bottom of the device at the thinnest point, excluding the camera.</li>
            	
            		<li class="textblock__disclaimer-text" role="listitem"><br />27. Armor Aluminum frame does not include volume and side keys, SIM tray or camera lens barrel.</li>
            	
            		<li class="textblock__disclaimer-text" role="listitem"><br />28. The IP68 rating on Galaxy S26 Ultra, S26+ and S26 is based on lab test conditions for submersion in up to 1.5 meters of freshwater for up to 30 minutes. No ingress of dust; complete protection against contact (dust-tight). Water and dust resistance of device is not permanent and may diminish over time because of normal wear and tear.</li>
            	
            		<li class="textblock__disclaimer-text" role="listitem"><br />29. Compared to previous Galaxy Z Fold models.</li>
            	
            		<li class="textblock__disclaimer-text" role="listitem"><br />30. Compared to previous Galaxy Z Flip models.</li>
            	
            		<li class="textblock__disclaimer-text" role="listitem"><br />31. Measured diagonally, Galaxy Z Flip7's Cover Screen size is 4.1” in the full rectangular form; actual viewable area is less due to the rounded corners and camera hole. </li>
            	
            		<li class="textblock__disclaimer-text" role="listitem"><br />32. The new wider woofer on Galaxy Buds4 Pro has 19.8% larger diaphragm compared to Galaxy Buds3 Pro.</li>
            	
            		<li class="textblock__disclaimer-text" role="listitem"><br />33. Ultra High Quality Audio up to 24-bit / 96 kHz is available on Galaxy S26 Series, S25 Series, S24 Series, S23 Series, Z Fold7, Z Flip7, Z Fold6, Z Flip6, Z Fold5, Z Flip5 and Tab S11 Series, Tab S10 Series, Tab S9 Series with One UI 6.1.1 or above. Additional devices may be supported in the future.</li>
            	
            		<li class="textblock__disclaimer-text" role="listitem"><br />34. UHQ is off by default and can be configured directly in the phone settings for devices running One UI 8.0 and later. For devices running on earlier versions of One UI, configurations can be found in the Galaxy Wearable app.</li>
            	
            		<li class="textblock__disclaimer-text" role="listitem"><br />35. Super Clear Call is available on Galaxy S26 Series, S25 Series, Z Fold7, Z Flip7, Z Fold6, Z Flip6, A56, Tab S11 Series and Tab S10 Series with One UI 6.1.1 or above. Additional devices may be supported in the future. Super Wideband (SWB) is available regardless of the Call App. SWB may not be supported depending on the mobile network between devices.</li>
            	
            		<li class="textblock__disclaimer-text" role="listitem"><br />36. Galaxy devices each sold separately.</li>
            	
            		<li class="textblock__disclaimer-text" role="listitem"><br />37. For general use of Samsung Notes between devices, network or Wi-Fi connection is required. All devices must be logged in to the same Samsung account. Not available on wearable devices. Working on shared notes as a group is available only on Galaxy Phone and Tab with Android O OS or higher. Requires the latest app update to Samsung Notes app.</li>
            	
            		<li class="textblock__disclaimer-text" role="listitem"><br />38. Available on Samsung Health app v.6.24 or above and must be paired with Samsung Galaxy smartphones with Android OS 11 and above. Samsung account login required.</li>
            	
            		<li class="textblock__disclaimer-text" role="listitem"><br />39. Intended for general wellness and fitness purposes only.</li>
            	
            		<li class="textblock__disclaimer-text" role="listitem"><br />40. Benefits may vary by product.</li>
            	
            		<li class="textblock__disclaimer-text" role="listitem"><br />41. To be eligible for trade-in, your qualifying device must meet all Trade-In Program eligibility requirements. For detailed information, please refer to https://www.samsung.com/pk/trade-in/.</li>
            	
            		<li class="textblock__disclaimer-text" role="listitem"><br />42. Measured diagonally, Galaxy S26 Ultra's screen size is 6.9” in the full rectangle and 6.7” accounting for the rounded corners; actual viewable area is less due to the rounded corners and camera hole.</li>
            	
            		<li class="textblock__disclaimer-text" role="listitem"><br />43. Measured diagonally, Galaxy Z Fold7’s Main Screen size is 8.0” in the full rectangle and 8.0” accounting for the rounded corners; actual viewable area is less due to the rounded corners.</li>
            	
            		<li class="textblock__disclaimer-text" role="listitem"><br />44. Now Nudge feature requires a Samsung Account login. Available functions and features may vary by country, region and language. Text message prompts available with certain third party messaging apps including Samsung Messages, Google Messages, Google Chat, WhatsApp, WhatsApp Business, KakaoTalk, LINE, Signal, Instagram (DM), Tango, NTT Docomo Messages, KDDI Messages. Share photos in Now Nudge works by analyzing available image content. Accuracy of results is not guaranteed.</li>
            	
            		<li class="textblock__disclaimer-text" role="listitem"><br />45. 50 MP resolution is available on Galaxy Z Flip7's rear wide camera only.</li>
            	
            		<li class="textblock__disclaimer-text" role="listitem"><br />46. Actual battery life varies by network environment, features and apps used, frequency of calls and messages, the number of times charged, and many other factors. Estimated against the average usage profile compiled by UX Connect Research. Independently assessed by UX Connect Research between 2025.06.12-2025.06.20 in US with pre-release versions of SM-F966 under default setting using LTE and 5G Sub6 networks. NOT tested under 5G mmWave Network.</li>
            	
            		<li class="textblock__disclaimer-text" role="listitem"><br />47. Actual battery life varies by network environment, features and apps used, frequency of calls and messages, the number of times charged, and many other factors. Estimated against the average usage profile compiled by UX Connect Research. Independently assessed by UX Connect Research between 2025.06.12-2025.06.20 in US with pre-release versions of SM-F766 under default setting using LTE and 5G Sub6 networks. NOT tested under 5G mmWave Network.</li>
            	
            		<li class="textblock__disclaimer-text" role="listitem"><br />48. Typical value tested under third-party laboratory condition. Typical value is the estimated average value considering the deviation in battery capacity among the battery samples tested under IEC 61960 standard. Rated capacity is 4175 mAh for Galaxy S26, 4755 mAh for Galaxy S26+, 4855 mAh for Galaxy S26 Ultra, 4272 mAh for Galaxy Z Fold7 and 4174 mAh for Galaxy Z Flip7.</li>
            	
            		<li class="textblock__disclaimer-text" role="listitem"><br />49. Based on lab test conditions for submersion in up to 1.5 meters of freshwater for up to 30 minutes. No ingress of dust; complete protection against contact (dust-tight). Water and dust resistance of device is not permanent and may diminish over time because of normal wear and tear.</li>
            	
            		<li class="textblock__disclaimer-text" role="listitem"><br />50. Measured diagonally, Galaxy Z Fold7's Cover Screen size is 6.5” in the full rectangle and 6.5” accounting for the rounded corners; actual viewable area is smaller due to the rounded corners and camera hole.</li>
            	
            		<li class="textblock__disclaimer-text" role="listitem"><br />51. Some functional widgets may require a network connection and/or Samsung Account login. Availability of functions supported within the apps may vary by country.</li>
            	
            		<li class="textblock__disclaimer-text" role="listitem"><br />52. Compatible smartphones and available features may vary by country/region, carrier or device.</li>
            	
            		<li class="textblock__disclaimer-text" role="listitem"><br />53. Each earbud contains three microphones (six in total across the device). The advanced DNN technology processes audio independently on each earbud, with no interaction between them.</li>
            	</ul>
			</div>
		</div>
	</div>
	

